        "original_id": "e737af7e-2200-5f78-ab3b-b6706cf48fcc",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Kyosuke Himuro, Boy George\n- Organizations: Boøwy\n- Places: Takasaki, Gunma, Japan\n- Roles: singer-songwriters, musicians, DJ, fashion designer, photographer, lead vocalist\n- Events: 1980s global hit songs\n\nFacts:\n- Kyosuke Himuro was born on October 7, 1960 in Takasaki, Gunma, Japan.\n- Kyosuke Himuro is a Japanese singer-songwriter and musician.\n- Boy George, born George Alan O'Dowd, was born on 14 June 1961.\n- Boy George is an English singer, songwriter, DJ, fashion designer, and photographer.\n- Kyosuke Himuro was the lead vocalist of the rock band Boøwy from 1981 to 1988.\n- During the 1980s, Boy George's band recorded global hit songs including \"Do You Really Want to Hurt Me,\" \"Time (Clock of the Heart),\" and \"Karma Chameleon.\"\n- Boy George is known for his soulful voice and androgynous appearance.",
